  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">VPSHR implementation for Trans-Adriatic Pipeline (TAP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ensure TAP, its contractors, security sub-contractors and relevant host state security are in compliance with international security convention, corporate security best practice, and TAP&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122;s policies and contractual requirements with suppliers. This is to be achieved by:oTraining TAP Security staff and security management of TAP&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122;s contractors so they can train security sub-contractorsoTraining police / state security forces where possible as requested by TAP SecurityoInspecting security sub-contractor training to ensure it is conducted adequatelyoProviding annual refresher training courses for all previously trained staff</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To support Voluntary Principles (&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2dc;VPs&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122;) training and implementation at corporate level (Switzerland) and across its three-country pipeline route (Greece, Albania and Italy).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trans-Adriatic Pipeline (TAP) and subcontractors</narrative>
  </description>
